Z||000000||Eddie.H||03-28-2000||08:02 PM||||1) CAN I put a GT speedo, RPM gage and the two little gages that sit on top of the raido in my SC? 2) are the clips  with the wires already there? I am using an after market RPM gage right now but I can get the GT stuff from a friend for free but if it it will need to be wired up then the hick with it my car is in a mess right now. Thanks Eddie||||reg||5
Z||000001||kevin||03-29-2000||01:19 AM||||Hey Eddie, I posted the same question last week for my 85 Duke. Momkeyman said the job is a simple plug and play. He said the center pod has to be wired but it is just as possible the plug has been supplied by Pontiac. We, (I said we because I haven't pulled my dash yet either) need to find wiring directions from Haynes or another souce. It was mentioned that this schematic was posted in the past on this Forum by batboy. Perhaps he can come to our mutual rescue.good luck. Isn't this Forum the BOMB!!||||reg||12
Z||000002||batboy||03-29-2000||12:54 PM||||Supposedly, 86 and newer Fiero "should" be wired for the ralley gauges. If not, you can still splice them in. Apparently the 84 models have a wire or two that are different from what I described in my tech article. Anyway, follow the below listed link to go to this topic to see what I did with my 85 SE Batmobile.<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/001538.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/001538.html</A> ||||reg||1
